From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] output: apply every fixed mode from output-management

wlr-output-management clients may select any fixed mode, not only the
connector's preferred mode. Converting a non-preferred fixed mode through
the zeroed custom_mode fields makes Phoc fall back to the preferred mode,
so runtime 60/90 Hz switching appears to succeed but does not change the
actual CRTC timing.

Use head->state.mode whenever a fixed mode is present. custom_mode remains
the fallback for clients that explicitly request a custom timing.
---
--- a/src/output.c
+++ b/src/output.c
@@ -1943,7 +1943,7 @@ phoc_output_config_head_to_output_config
   PhocOutputConfig *oc = phoc_output_config_new (phoc_output_get_identifier (self));
 
   oc->enable = TRUE;
-  if (head->state.mode && head->state.mode->preferred) {
+  if (head->state.mode) {
     oc->mode.width = head->state.mode->width;
     oc->mode.height = head->state.mode->height;
     oc->mode.refresh_rate = head->state.mode->refresh / 1000.0;
